<div class="content-box" style="background: #fff3cd; border-left: 4px solid #ffc107;">
    <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-lightbulb"></i> Watch Out For</h2>
    <p>Common misconceptions to avoid:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>NoSQL vs. SQL: Believing NoSQL is "better." It is a trade-off: NoSQL offers scaling and flexibility but usually sacrifices strict ACID compliance.</li>
        <li>Distributed Consistency: Thinking data is updated everywhere instantly; students must understand "Eventual Consistency."</li>
        <li>Data Mining: Confusing it with a standard search. Mining is about discovering unknown patterns, not finding specific records.</li>
    </ul>
</div>

